#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:1
msgid "Alternatives and Prior Art"
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:3
msgid ""
"There is no shortage of command runners! Some more or less similar "
"alternatives to `just` include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:6
msgid ""
"[make](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Make_(software)): The Unix build tool "
"that inspired `just`. There are a few different modern day descendants of "
"the original `make`, including [FreeBSD Make](https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/"
"man.cgi?make(1)) and [GNU Make](https://www.gnu.org/software/make/)."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:11
msgid ""
"[task](https://github.com/go-task/task): A YAML-based command runner written "
"in Go."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:13
msgid ""
"[maid](https://github.com/egoist/maid): A Markdown-based command runner "
"written in JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:15
msgid ""
"[microsoft/just](https://github.com/microsoft/just): A JavaScript-based "
"command runner written in JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:17
msgid ""
"[cargo-make](https://github.com/sagiegurari/cargo-make): A command runner "
"for Rust projects."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:19
msgid ""
"[mmake](https://github.com/tj/mmake): A wrapper around `make` with a number "
"of improvements, including remote includes."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:21
msgid ""
"[robo](https://github.com/tj/robo): A YAML-based command runner written in "
"Go."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:23
msgid ""
"[mask](https://github.com/jakedeichert/mask): A Markdown-based command "
"runner written in Rust."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:25
msgid ""
"[makesure](https://github.com/xonixx/makesure): A simple and portable "
"command runner written in AWK and shell."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:27
msgid ""
"[haku](https://github.com/VladimirMarkelov/haku): A make-like command runner "
"written in Rust."
msgstr ""

#: src/alternatives-and-prior-art.md:29
msgid ""
"[mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/): A development environment tool manager "
"written in Rust supporting tasks in TOML files and standalone scripts."
msgstr ""
